        },
        {
          "node_type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "node_type": "text",
              "value": "When you use a reach spell-like ability, it can alter a spell-like ability with a range of touch, close, or medium to increase its range to a higher range category, using the following order: touch, close, medium, and long. You can select a spell-like ability that duplicates a spell only if its level is less than or equal to 1/2 its caster level (round down) – 1 per increase in range category. For example, a spell-like ability with a range of touch can be increased to long range only if it duplicates a spell with a level less than or equal to 1/2 your caster level (round down) – 3. For a summary, see Table 3–3. Reach spell-like abilities that normally require melee touch attacks instead require ranged touch attacks."
            }
